WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.340
- All right let's talk about Bill Cosby

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:02.650
and why he's going free.

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:03.810
This is a complicated issue,

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:06.280
but the short version is
not that he's innocent,

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:08.210
but that he was effectively tricked

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:09.506
into waiving his fifth amendment rights

00:00:09.506 --> 00:00:11.601
and that made his conviction infirm.

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:12.850
Background is this,

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:13.683
in 2005,

00:00:13.683 --> 00:00:15.010
Andrea Constand came forward

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:17.180
with rape allegations against Bill Cosby.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.039
This was a few years
after the incident itself.

00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:22.216
She delayed for personal reasons.

00:00:22.216 --> 00:00:23.770
The District Attorney,

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:25.370
who we'll come back to in a second,

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:27.050
decided not to prosecute.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:28.340
Remember this is in 2005

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:31.128
before scores of women
came forward against Cosby.

00:00:31.128 --> 00:00:32.590
And it was not clear that

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:33.830
the prosecutors would be able to get

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:35.040
a conviction against him.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.150
So the District Attorney,

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:36.983
Bruce Castor,

00:00:36.983 --> 00:00:38.970
who is now famous for
representing President Trump

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:40.050
in the impeachment hearings,

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.950
decided to issue a promise

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.330
to Cosby that they weren't going

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:44.750
to go forward with prosecuting him,

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:46.153
continued in part two.

